From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:29:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] cli: use bundled tsrs for application typechecking

Ship a pinned tsrs runtime dependency and use it for every configured
application check. Resolve its launcher relative to the installed SDK,
including bundled CommonJS and nested package-manager layouts. Remove the
compiler selector and obsolete project-local TypeScript version probe.

Always disable emission, preserve watched-file registration and concurrent
edit retries, and wait for diagnostic pipes to close before reporting a
failed check. Accept an empty project only when its no-inputs diagnostic
is the sole reported error.

Retain the existing enable, try and disable modes and the SDK declaration
baseline. Older tsc-based clients remain backend-compatible because the
checker does not change deployment requests or emitted JavaScript.
